This work builds on, and does not modify, the following:

- Xi Chen, Ce Jin, Tim Randolph and Rocco A. Servedio, arXiv 2301.07134: the Representation-OV algorithm of their
  Sec. 4, its model, constants (Equations (3), (4)), Lemmas 2, 3, 5, 6, 8, Observations 1, 2, 4, footnote 8, and the
  cost accounting of their Theorem 2. Stage 1 replaces only their random prime and their s(l) random residues.
- Ye and Li, arXiv 2610.10446 (v1): the prefix representation, layers, partial-match subroutine and hardcoded
  circuit (Cor. 3.2, Cor. 3.3), the few-sums branch, the exponent table of Sec. 4, and Prop. 4.2. Stage 2 replaces
  only their randomized filter and repetitions.
- Alman and Li (AL25), arXiv 2509.14489 (FOCS 2025): Thm B.2, used inside Ye-Li Prop. 4.2 (Thm 6.1, which
  Prop. 4.2 also cites, is replaced here by proofs/stage2.md Lemma 9.1).
- Per Austrin, Petteri Kaski, Mikko Koivisto and Jesper Nederlof (AKKN16), Lemma 3.2: the few-sums branch.
- Ellis Horowitz and Sartaj Sahni, JACM 1974: meet-in-the-middle.
- Greedy set cover: David S. Johnson 1974, László Lovász 1975, Vašek Chvátal 1979 (Lemma 2.3 of Stage 1).
- OpenAI, openai/math preprint (October 2026): the randomized 2^{0.489995 n} Subset Sum construction (#138); our
  randomness audit of it led to the covering tool used here. It is not derandomised here.
- Lixi Ye and Baitian Li's unpublished "Record 3" reduction (Stages 4 to 5b). Only its numerical candidate
  0.499664500303... is public, in the AI-disclosure section of arXiv 2610.10446 v1, which credits the reduction to an
  AI model inside their project and says its formal proof is pending there. Its specifics (the block representation,
  few/many sums on the block, the kappa layers, the balanced splits with cores at density s, the round count, the
  tensor circuit, the s-cancellation identity, the cost functions and saving coefficients, the one-pass covering
  circuit family, and the values xi(1/8), xi(0.11)) were read in Record 3's transcript, which the paper's AI-disclosure section links (https://chatgpt.com/share/6ac5a437-5d0c-83e8-afea-fcc450b322b0); we re-derived and
  re-certified all of them, and they remain Record 3's ideas.
- The (AL-B2) rebalancing statement as Ye and Li state it before their Lemma 3.4, extracted from Alman and Li's
  App. B (Stages 4 to 5b).
- Mathlib (leanprover-community) and Lean 4; the log-series bounds of lean/SubsetsumLean/Basic.lean are copied from
  unpublished code of the author and rest on Mathlib's Real.abs_log_sub_add_sum_range_le and Real.binEntropy.

New here: the deterministic prime with injectivity on W(C) (Stage 1 Lemma 2.1), the simultaneous bound on W'(T)
(Lemma 2.2), the universal residue covering over (restriction, shift) with the best rotation (Lemmas 2.3, 2.4) and
its use as a filter in both stages; the collision-bounded prime and residue-threshold layer families of Stage 2;
the re-derivation of Ye-Li's exponent at a general prefix and the choice pi = 0.2499; the inclusion-exclusion
replacement for Alman-Li Thm 6.1 (Stage 2 Sec. 9); the explicit construction of Stage 2b (pessimistic-estimator
lists, greedy hole fixing, the effective three-piece rebalancing rule, the preprocessing count); the smaller-n0
variants of Stage 2b Secs. 12-13 (the per-pair rebalancing constant, the halving splitter with the canonical-member
rule, the anchors at a new (a, b) by concavity, the positive union after the tree, the ladder of base lengths); the
certificates and their Lean kernel checks.

Also new here: the outside-sum dedupe and the re-tuned Ye-Li circuit of Stage 3; for Stages 4 to 5b, the proofs of
every step Record 3 left argued (the density-s Lemmas 3.1 and 3.4 with unbalanced queries, the left-degree
concentration, the balanced half-splits, the fixed round family with its multiplicity and loss), the repairs (the
filter cap, Phi's universe restricted to the good c, the prime p ~ T with the collision count, the parity bit, the
fixed-point estimator, the enumeration of compatible K, the poly(n, L) factors), the whole deterministic port, the
families of circuits on this route (Stage 4+ and Stage 5b, with Lemma 5b.1), the outer-sum dedupe and the
kappa-adaptive core menu of Stage 5, and all certificates, brute-force checks and Lean kernel checks.
